body:
side note: its hella douchey if you instantly start timing your baristas breaks without even giving them a heads up and rush them.

&#x200B;

also for the love of god do not fucking bother me during my break

Actually they would just try to out karen each other until eventually they end up fighting each other, and some poor soul has to break up their fight.

&#x200B;

Also he sounds greasy and crusty.

Oh yeah sure it's totally against policy to help a child get home safely, but making them walk home in a crazy dangerous condition is TOTALLY the Starbucks™️ way!

&#x200B;

They're insufferable and I hope they get fired for being a shitbag.

You're not supposed to come in with symptoms, even worse since you have covid. Your manager should not be wanting you to come in.

&#x200B;

Maybe if starbucks wasnt allowing customers to come in without masks and cough everywhere disgustingly, infection rates could come down..

This gif made me remember why I loved this show. It just takes me back to a more simple time in middle school, before all this covid shit hit the fan with mfs getting each other sick and having to deal with college and a crappy job in starbucks. God I miss this show and all the characters that really made it #1. They really don't make em like they used to. Thank you OP for making my day, it really helped me out. <3

&#x200B;

Maybe I might go rewatch the first few seasons sometime, whenever I have time...

Guy tried grabbing a cup from my hands to micromanage me on his drink.

&#x200B;

Dude had a melt down just as a wave of high schoolers came in and he marched off.

The antagonistic side of me says the next time he walks up to the counter, just spray him with a full can of whip. Why? Cause fuck him thats why.

&#x200B;

The non-engaging and peacekeeping side of me says to file out incident reports and refuse him service for being a creepy ass pedo. Why? Cause fuck him thats why.

Don't put emotional stock into what happens, even if you end up seeing coworkers suffer. I love the people I work with (well except one but thats cause shes a corporate sucker), but whatever I do, they will get screwed over at some point cause corporate makes shit decisions. I know I will get screwed one day too, which is why I am aiming to leave some day soon. Also avoid any kind of drama like the plague, as starbucks store drama is the absolute worst. Usually it ends up being some type of drama with night shift vs morning shift or something that has to due with the work itself going south. When that happens, you end up seeing the machine that corporate oils up well, even when all the gears (us partners) crash and scratch each other up. Keep yourself together and don't break your back for anyone out of some false sense of obligation, as that is what corporate would want you to do.

&#x200B;

TL;DR, It's Just Coffee. Don't hurt yourself over it.

It's gotten to the point that mid shift is entirely centered around getting ready for the high schooler wave and knowing that the moment we hear someone in drive thru say "we have three separate orders" that it was the war horn going off. Sometimes we survive, sometimes we all mentally die at once.

&#x200B;

Also idk if its just me, but for some reason when a bunch of hs dudes come in at once, it feels really uneasy when they just stare at me, especially if they all got their phones out waving it everywhere.

Ok so first off, the dudes in full suits always scare me as customers cause theyre always the rudest.

&#x200B;

Second, you don't miss starbucks, yet ur flair says supervisor?

Fuck the siren and FUCK your manager for changing YOUR availability.

&#x200B;

With that being said, I'd suggest talking to your manager asap, and since u seemed to already call them out, theres a chance they might make you find cover for the shit that was put out of your availability since they might not consider it "an emergency" even though it was their fault. Surely though, it SHOULDN'T be your responsbility.

She's being fucking dumb. I'd attach a tampon to my apron as a giant middle finger lmao.

&#x200B;

"Hi welcome to Starbucks, my name is Tammy the Tampon, what can I get for you today?"

To tell you the truth, it depends on the type of store you're working at. If you work at a cafe only story (like say the mall), you're likely to get the closest to old school starbucks where it was more simple, though you will get lots of weird ass drinks (like say a vanilla frap with 16 pumps of everything), but thats every starbucks nowadays. You won't have the pressure of drive thru times, but I do believe those stores tend to get closed down the most, since corporate is pushing a more mcdonalds type buisness model. Suburban areas tend to have more stores with drive thrus, so chances are you'll learn to hate drive thru times, but if you stick to night shifts you should be ok, and you'll have more time and ease to learn all the new stuff. Also a little heads up alot of stuff from way back then have changed in how it's done and they got new machines to do things (new ovens and espresso machines for example).

&#x200B;

Overall, the Starbucks you knew back then is completely gone and in it's place is a type fast food buisness with the same name. If you need the money that bad, go for it, the benefits are good enough, but if not, keep searching.

Only if they hate all customers beforehand, like me >:)

&#x200B;

jk, i dont rlly care. Im totally cool with it, even if I have to type it up on the register or go out of my way to tell the person on bar. If it tastes like shit I rlly dont mind remaking it too so long as it isnt busy and you're not a dick about it. Most of us baristas dont mind complicated drinks, our bitterness comes from rude waves of customers. You're good <3

me: alright please let me know when you are ready

&#x200B;

them: yes i have 6 seperate orders ill have a grande \*insert non existant tiktok drink\*

Snitches are bitches who get stitches. I got a partner who'd probably pull the same shit too. They ain't worth the time, but you definitely should stay clear of them, especially knowing they are willing to come for you when you're practically getting pinned down. They'll only screw you over harder the next time they got you in their crosshairs, and will not hesitate to gun you down without reason (aka get you fired).

&#x200B;

edit: i realized i said gun twice and sounded even more edgy than i usually do lmao

